{:doc "Rows of tests/conformance/corpus.edn (:common) that fail on cleat, each classified. tools/conformance.clj --gate fails on a NEW failing row and on a STALE entry."
 :counts {:corpus/jolt-value 98, :error-model 6, :host/boxing 3, :host/class-name 17, :host/defaults 1, :host/exception-type 28, :host/hash 2, :host/jvm-api 310, :host/message 2, :host/numeric-types 10, :host/reader-features 4, :host/regex 39, :host/strings 1, :not-yet 27, :numeric 2, :printf 2, :strictness 2, :upstream/clojureclr 7}
 :legend
 {:host/jvm-api
  "the row calls a Java API: java.* / javax.* classes, java.lang statics (Long/MAX_VALUE, Integer/parseInt, Double/isNaN, System/getProperty), Java method names (.getMessage, .length, .getName, .substring), java.io / clojure.java.io, or clojure.lang members by their JVM names. cleat runs on the CLR and does not emulate the Java class library (designs/03 §4); the CLR spelling (.Message, Int64/MaxValue, clojure.clr.io …) works"
  :host/class-name
  "the value is a class name or a printed Class: CLR names (System.String, Outer+Inner, TypedArraySeq`1) instead of java.lang.String / Outer$Inner; (str (class x)) has no \"class \" prefix"
  :host/exception-type
  "the JVM throws a specific java.lang exception (NullPointerException, ClassCastException, AssertionError, ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException …) where cleat throws the CLR exception it actually raises (ArgumentNullException, a Reflector overload miss, IndexOutOfRangeException …) that the JVM-name alias does not cover, or the message is .NET's; see designs/03 §4 for the alias table"
  :host/regex
  "java.util.regex syntax or semantics that System.Text.RegularExpressions does not share: \\Q…\\E, possessive quantifiers, POSIX \\p{Alpha}, \\p{javaUpperCase}, (?u), class intersection [a&&b], \\R, \\x{…}, \\c edge cases, look-behind bounds"
  :host/numeric-types
  "CLR numeric types: byte is System.Byte (unsigned 0..255), the narrowing / unchecked casts use .NET's rules (char accepted as its code, no sign folding for byte)"
  :host/hash
  "Object.hashCode-based results (hash-combine's Util/hash, format %h on non-strings): ClojureCLR's Util.hash is hasheq, and CLR GetHashCode differs from Java's hashCode"
  :host/reader-features
  "cleat reads #? / #?@ with the :cljr feature (like ClojureCLR), so :clj branches are not taken"
  :host/boxing
  "identity of boxed values: CLR boxes of equal numbers / interned strings are distinct objects (the JVM caches small Longs and interns symbol names)"
  :host/strings
  "string predicates use .NET character classes (Char.IsWhiteSpace) rather than Java's"
  :host/message
  "the same exception with a ClojureCLR / .NET message text"
  :host/defaults
  "a default that is host-specific (*compile-path*)"
  :printf
  "gaps in clojure.lang.Printf, ClojureCLR's port of java.util.Formatter that format / printf use"
  :numeric
  "numeric printing / conversion detail that differs from the JVM (subnormal digits in %e, rationalize of a double)"
  :strictness
  "cleat accepts an argument the JVM rejects (a superset)"
  :error-model
  "compile errors are one ExpanderException whose message carries the position (\"Syntax error (file:line:col) …\"), not a CompilerException wrapping a cause; ex-cause / message texts differ (cleat-055 error model)"
  :upstream/clojureclr
  "cleat's src/clojure is ClojureCLR's core (Clojure 1.13 alpha); the corpus is Clojure 1.12.5: *clojure-version*, select-keys via get, destructure's :or hoisting, array-map growth"
  :corpus/jolt-value
  "the row's :expected is jolt's own value, not reference Clojure's: listed in jolt's known-divergences.edn or in jolt's profile.edn with a non-certified bucket (:jvm-raises, :uncertifiable, :divergent, :read-error …), names that are not clojure.core (atom?, regex?, sorted-set? …), or files from jolt's repository"
  :not-yet
  "a gap cleat intends to close; the reason names the target task"}
